From f3f03b2035bec4bc1c8a80288789ea3c7d54f383 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 05:41:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hir/from_ast: a bound associated type defined in a parent
 trait reached through an omitted default parameter

simba 0.8.1 (librsvg 2.58.5, nalgebra) src/scalar/real.rs:24-25
`pub trait RealField: ComplexField<RealField = Self> + RelativeEq<Epsilon = Self> + UlpsEq<Epsilon = Self> + ..`:
"BUG: ASSERT FAIL: src/hir_typeck/common.cpp:685: Type param Rhs/*I:0*/ out of range for (max 0)".

approx 0.5.1 defines `Epsilon` in `AbsDiffEq<Rhs = Self>`; `RelativeEq<Rhs = Self>: AbsDiffEq<Rhs>` and
`UlpsEq<Rhs = Self>: AbsDiffEq<Rhs>` reach it through their own parameter, and the bindings omit `Rhs`.
LowerHIR_TraitPath records which trait a bound's associated type belongs to (find_source_trait) by
monomorphising the parent's path with the parameters as written - none here - while defaults are only
filled in by Resolve Bind, so the `Rhs` of `AbsDiffEq<Rhs>` had nothing to map to.

The omitted parameters now take the trait's defaults (`Rhs = Self`), monomorphised with the type the path
bounds as `Self`: LowerHIR_TraitPath gets a `self_ty` argument (a generic bound's type, `Self` for a
supertrait, the erased self of `dyn`/`impl Trait`), which is also what a `Self` named by the parent path
itself now means. `trait RealField: RelativeEq<Epsilon = Self>` records `AbsDiffEq<Self>`,
`fn f<T: RelativeEq<Epsilon = T>>` records `AbsDiffEq<T>`, and `T: Child2<Self, Out2 = T>` in a trait
method (written `Self` next to the omitted default) records `Parent2<Self, T>`. The HIR and AST walks and
the two trait-alias branches share the filling; the external trait-alias branch mapped the alias's traits
with the caller's monomorphiser instead of the alias path's own parameters, fixed in passing.

`fn mk() -> impl RelativeEq<Epsilon = F>` now reaches an older, separate bug: every `impl Trait` return
whose trait has a `Self` default (`-> impl PartialEq`) fails at its first call site with "Generic binding
out of total range (ErasedSelf)" (C228).

Assisted-By: Claude Fable 5.1
---

